  "reasoning": "The facts show that the defendant accepted large sums of money in exchange for using his influence with a public official to obtain project contracts and mining rights (受贿). He also paid bribes to public officials (薛某、林某1、曾某) to obtain favorable treatment, which constitutes 行贿. In the case of the 35万元, the bribe was paid by the defendant’s company (宏图公司) on its behalf, which is classified as 对单位行贿. No contract fraud or bribery of non‑state persons is described, so the appropriate charges are 受贿, 行贿, and 对单位行贿.",
  "final_answer": "[罪名]受贿;行贿;对单位行贿<eoa>"
}
